.SS "typedef void(* p6est_replace_t) (\fBp6est_t\fP *\fBp6est\fP, \fBp4est_topidx_t\fP which_tree, int num_outcolumns, int num_outlayers, \fBp4est_quadrant_t\fP *outcolumns[], \fBp2est_quadrant_t\fP *outlayers[], int num_incolumns, int num_inlayers, \fBp4est_quadrant_t\fP *incolumns[], \fBp2est_quadrant_t\fP *inlayers[])"

.PP
Callback function prototype to transfer information from outgoing layers to incoming layers\&. This is used by extended routines when the layers of an existing, valid \fBp6est\fP are changed\&. The callback allows the user to make changes to newly initialized layers before the layers that they replace are destroyed\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fInum_outcolumns\fP The number of columns that contain the outgoing layers: will be either 1 or 4\&. 
.br
\fInum_outlayers\fP The number of outgoing layers: will be either 1 (a single layer is being refined), 2 (two layers are being vertically coarsened), or 4 (four layers are being horizontally coarsened)\&. 
.br
\fIoutcolumns\fP The columns of the outgoing layers 
.br
\fIoutlayers\fP The outgoing layers: after the callback, the user_data, if \fIp6est->data_size\fP is nonzero, will be destroyed\&. 
.br
\fInum_incolumns\fP The number of columns that contain the outgoing layers: will be either 1 or 4\&. 
.br
\fInum_inlayers\fP The number of incoming layers: will be either 1 (coarsening), 2 (vertical refinement), or 4 (horizontal refinement) 
.br
\fIincolumns\fP The columns of the incoming layers 
.br
\fIinlayers\fP The incoming layers: prior to the callback, the user_data, if \fIp6est->data_size\fP is nonzero, is allocated, and the p6est_init_t callback, if it has been provided, will be called\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "typedef int(* p6est_weight_t) (\fBp6est_t\fP *\fBp6est\fP, \fBp4est_topidx_t\fP which_tree, \fBp4est_quadrant_t\fP *column, \fBp2est_quadrant_t\fP *layer)"

.PP
Callback function prototype to calculate weights for partitioning\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
a 32bit integer >= 0 as the quadrant weight\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Global sum of weights must fit into a 64bit integer\&. 
.RE
.PP

