.SS "\fBp6est_connectivity_t\fP* p6est_connectivity_new (\fBp4est_connectivity_t\fP * conn4, double * top_vertices, double height[3])"

.PP
Create a p6est_connectivity_t from a p4est_connectivity_t\&. All fields are copied, so all inputs can be safey destroyed\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIconn4\fP the 2D connectivity 
.br
\fItop_vertices\fP if NULL, then the sheet has a uniform vertical profile; otherwise, \fItop_vertices\fP gives the vertices of the top of the sheet; should be the same size as \fIconn4->tree_to_vertex\fP 
.br
\fIheight\fP if \fItop_vertices\fP == NULL, then this gives the offset from the bottom of the sheet to the top\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
the 2D+1D connectivity information\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBp6est_t\fP* p6est_copy (\fBp6est_t\fP * input, int copy_data)"

.PP
Make a deep copy of a \fBp6est\fP\&. The connectivity is not duplicated\&. Copying of quadrant user data is optional\&. If old and new data sizes are 0, the user_data field is copied regardless\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIcopy_data\fP If true, data are copied\&. If false, data_size is set to 0\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Returns a valid \fBp6est\fP that does not depend on the input\&. 
.RE
.PP

