.SS "\fBp6est_t\fP* p6est_new (sc_MPI_Comm mpicomm, \fBp6est_connectivity_t\fP * connectivity, size_t data_size, \fBp6est_init_t\fP init_fn, void * user_pointer)"

.PP
Create a new forest\&. The new forest consists of equi-partitioned root quadrants\&. When there are more processors than trees, some processors are empty\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImpicomm\fP A valid MPI communicator\&. 
.br
\fIconnectivity\fP This is the connectivity information that the forest is built with\&. Note the \fBp6est\fP does not take ownership of the memory\&. 
.br
\fIdata_size\fP This is the size of data for each quadrant which can be zero\&. Then user_data_pool is set to NULL\&. 
.br
\fIinit_fn\fP Callback function to initialize the user_data which is already allocated automatically\&. 
.br
\fIuser_pointer\fP Assign to the user_pointer member of the \fBp6est\fP before init_fn is called the first time\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This returns a valid forest\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The connectivity structure must not be destroyed during the lifetime of this forest\&. 
.RE
.PP

